{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1004276-did-the-children-of-gaia-help-create-the-hippy-movement-and-woodstock","id":1004276,"title":"Did the Children of Gaia help create The Hippy Movement and Woodstock?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-17T00:01:10-08:00","id":1004276,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon6.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Did the Children of Gaia help create The Hippy Movement and Woodstock?","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\">In the process of drawing a &quot;Beatles&quot; inspired Manga its inevitable you start doing cultural/historical research for stylistic-design inspirations, and then it hit me.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Waging War against hate with peace, love, friendship, tolerance and hope; Embracing Pagan and non-western-cultures and ways of living, communing with The Earth Mother through Herbal Smoke...&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Surely, The Children of Gaia were Instrumental in creating The Hippy Movement as a last-ditched blunt-force resistance against Richard Nixon's War on Human Decency/Dignity, with Woodstock as an (unfortunately failed) attempt to Part-The-Veil en-mass to a legion of Loving-Kind-Loving-Tolerant-and-Hopeful Children, and in the First Step to Opening The Next Generation of Humanity's Collective Soul to Gaia?<br /> <br /> On that note;<br /> Would describing The Sea of Monsters from &quot;The Yellow Submarine&quot; to Players Stepping-Sideways for the very first time he a good analogy of the psychedelic madness of the umbra to to un-initiated?<br /> All I can say after seeing it was<br /> <br /> (1) Beatles Rule, Man!<br /> (2) I don't think I ever need to TRY Acid after this cos SURELY this is what it would look like<br /> (3) Hard Day's Night is still the better Beatles Film. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Peace Out, Man! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 11-17-2016, 03:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T01:32:10-08:00","id":1004293,"title":"","content":"I think that the CoG were heavily motivated by the Hippie movement at least as a design influence.<br /> No one group is ever responsible for any human movement. The counter-culture movement may have in the WoD been influenced by: The Children of Gaia, The Dreamspeakers, Verbena, Cult of Escatsy, Toreador, Brujah, and Followers of Set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T01:51:52-08:00","id":1004295,"title":"","content":"Nixon's cronies would no doubt have had a Lasombra and Shadow Lord or three among its numbers to allow him to drag out the misery of the Vietnam War over his 6 years of tyranny, and have Lennon assassinated another 6 later to end the Era of Hope, that worthless warmongering Wyrm-bastard. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T14:43:41-08:00","id":1004642,"title":"","content":"Supernatural involvement or creation of real history is something that tends to alienate people when it is in published material, but often seen as cool or interesting when done selectively in actual home chronicles (especially if the players are somehow involved).<br /> <br /> Rather than saying the Children of Gaia created the Hippie Movement, I think it would be more accurate to say that the Children of Gaia's <i>kinfolk</i> were very <i>active</i> within the Hippie Movement.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you want to trace back the origins of the Hippies you eventually get to the German naturists (it was the Germans who invented the term ecology and began its study, and the Wandervogel movement of the 1920s was very similar to the hippies in many ways). Of course, the Garou kinfolk most likely to be involved with that in Germany were, of course, ...those of the Get of Fenris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T18:30:27-08:00","id":1004736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1004276-did-the-children-of-gaia-help-create-the-hippy-movement-and-woodstock?p=1004642#post1004642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernatural involvement or creation of real history is something that tends to alienate people when it is in published material, but often seen as cool or interesting when done selectively in actual home chronicles (especially if the players are somehow involved).<br /> <br /> Rather than saying the Children of Gaia created the Hippie Movement, I think it would be more accurate to say that the Children of Gaia's <i>kinfolk</i> were very <i>active</i> within the Hippie Movement.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you want to trace back the origins of the Hippies you eventually get to the German naturists (it was the Germans who invented the term ecology and began its study, and the Wandervogel movement of the 1920s was very similar to the hippies in many ways). Of course, the Garou kinfolk most likely to be involved with that in Germany were, of course, ...those of the Get of Fenris.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or the Shadow Lords. Or the Silver Fangs. Or the Bone Gnawers. Or the Glass Walkers. Just like how Ireland doesn't just have Fianna, Germany didn't just have the Get; this is even referenced in the origin of Evan Stump, whose BSD kin ancestors fled from Germany with the Shadow Lords on their heels.<br /> <br /> (The BSDs, of course, are everywhere, but I omitted them for a fairly obvious reason).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T18:41:25-08:00","id":1004741,"title":"","content":"*bursts into thread, panting*<br /> <br /> Jesus of Nazareth, who is called Christ, the Son of God, is canonically Children of Gaia kinfolk. Remember this when you ask whether to include supernatural influence on real history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T19:19:01-08:00","id":1004756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1004276-did-the-children-of-gaia-help-create-the-hippy-movement-and-woodstock?p=1004293#post1004293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one group is ever responsible for any human movement...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernatural involvement or creation of real history is something that tends to alienate people... ...Rather than saying the Children of Gaia created the Hippie Movement, I think it would be more accurate to say that the Children of Gaia's <i>kinfolk</i> were very <i>active</i> within the Hippie Movement.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhat they said -- mostly. I've found that when figuring out how much supernaturals in World of Darkness have affected major historical events, a major counter argument is that &quot;Well, these things happened in the <i>real world</i>, so it <i>can't </i>be due to the influence of the werewolves, vampires, mages, etc. because it would have happened anyway&quot;. And at the risk of restarting some past flame-wars on this very topic, I would say that in the World of Darkness, there are forces at play that do not apply to the real world. With that in mind, I'd say that that right there invalidates this line of reasoning, and leaves the door open for supernaturals (also being forces not at play in our own world) to have an influence on the history of the World of Darkness that far outstrips their apparent influence (on first bounce) given how closely WoD hews to our own reality.<br /> <br /> \u200bGiven how closely some of the Hippie Movement and things like Woodstock cleave to Child of Gaia ideals, I don't see it as unreasonable that the tribe (including the Garou) would (or at least could) have had a direct role in those things. To say that the 60s and all that went with it somehow created the tribe in its modern form doesn't make much sense to me given that the tribe was already pretty much like that before that time.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jesus of Nazareth, who is called Christ, the Son of God, is canonically Children of Gaia kinfolk.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bUm... yeah, according to the <i>Children of Gaia</i>. Remember also that Frederick Law Olmstead is simultaneously claimed by like, three different tribes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T20:50:02-08:00","id":1004787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1004276-did-the-children-of-gaia-help-create-the-hippy-movement-and-woodstock?p=1004642#post1004642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, if you want to trace back the origins of the Hippies you eventually get to the German naturists (it was the Germans who invented the term ecology and began its study, and the Wandervogel movement of the 1920s was very similar to the hippies in many ways). Of course, the Garou kinfolk most likely to be involved with that in Germany were, of course, ...those of the Get of Fenris.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, considering the fact that modern Get of Fenris feel a collective shame of having ancestors joining <b>Adolph Hitler</b> in his genocidal wars, it actually makes a lot of poignant sense that they would try to redeem themselves through trying to start a Culture/Religion of Love and Mercy.<br /> <br /> Heck, even Thunder-Tooth, the Lupus narrator for <i>Get of Fenris: Revised</i>, (bias towards Wendigo notwithstanding), breaks ALL stereotypes of the bloodthirsty berserker and is instead a warm, jolly and kind-hearted grandfather who is compassionate towards the weak and despises bullies... not unlike a Hippy, when you think about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 11-17-2016, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T13:11:21-08:00","id":1008655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1004276-did-the-children-of-gaia-help-create-the-hippy-movement-and-woodstock?p=1004787#post1004787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, considering the fact that modern Get of Fenris feel a collective shame of having ancestors joining <b>Adolph Hitler</b> in his genocidal wars, it actually makes a lot of poignant sense that they would try to redeem themselves through trying to start a Culture/Religion of Love and Mercy.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are actually missing my point so I may need to explain better. It is an ironic comment about how many things that influenced the hippies are not in fact intrinsically pacifistic or concerned with love and mercy. First, the Wandervogel movement and the general trend of a romantic back to nature movement predates, not postdates, the Nazis. And far from being antithetical to Nazism, was a deep influence on it. People of all sorts of political persuasion participated, including traditional conservatives and the Nazis as well as their opponents.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, far from being antithetical to Gaian perspectives, a strong argument can be made how the Nazis embody many kinds of Garou ideals. The Nazis were the first modern political movement to emphasize protection of the environment. The Nazis passed the first anti-pollution laws in the world and extended legal protection to animals. It was the first state to put the wolf under legal protection and passed various anti-cruelty to animals law. The Nazis believed in a very strong connection between the people and the earth they lived on (blood and soil), and even their racism can be seen as an analogue to Garou Pure Breeding. They strongly believed in the local community and folk traditions and were distrustful of modern industrial capitalism. Even things that we find abhorrent about the Nazis, are probably deeply supported by many elements in the Garou Nation. For example, the Nazi culling of the mentally and physically disabled fits within Garou notions that one does not let the people suffer to tend to their own sickness. (But of course, there have always been and still are Garou who supported the Impergium)<br /> <br /> In fact before 1941, when the Nazis began their true genocidal killings, quite a strong argument could be made by the German Get of Fenris that Nazism represented the best approximation of Gaian values in humanity since before the Impergium, and that a German attack (and victory) on the Soviet Union (which had murdered more people before their entry into the war than the Germans would murder during it) would represent a strong blow for Gaia in the same sense that in the initial invasion many Soviet citizens welcomed the Nazis as liberators.<br /> <br /> Instead, I think it shows no matter how an ideology looks like it includes and is compatible with various Gaian tenets can be corrupted by the Wyrm. One would think for all the shame heaped upon the Get about the Nazis, that the tribes whose kinfolk supported Bolshevism (particularly Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers, but even the Children of Gaia very early on) would be even more condemned (as they combined even higher body counts than the Nazis plus environmental devastation on a mass scale), but we don't see this in the books. This probably reflects more of a blindspot on the sourcebook authors, but in the setting is probably accounted for by 1) those tribes are already seen as suspect and thus Garou find them hopeless while they believe the Get can be shamed out of their worse aspects, and 2) the Silver Fangs don't want attention at their own huge failure in Russia concerning human politics so they make sure the Get are attacked as part of a <i>tu quoque</i> defense.<br /> <br /> As for the Hippies themselves, seeing them merely as innocent flower children involves ignoring a huge dark side. Many hippie communes broke down under the abuse (emotional, physical, sexual) and bullying of their leaders, or individuals destroyed by abuse of various drugs. And of course, the Manson family came out of the hippie culture as well. The Manson example is of course an extreme one, but many hippie communes self destructed for very real reasons. It's perfectly fine in your game to say, &quot;Well, that isn't truly hippie culture because it's not what I consider to be part of it&quot;; but those elements are still proof that the corruption of the Wyrm can strike anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T18:12:44-08:00","id":1008729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1004276-did-the-children-of-gaia-help-create-the-hippy-movement-and-woodstock?p=1008655#post1008655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the Hippies themselves, seeing them merely as innocent flower children involves ignoring a huge dark side. Many hippie communes broke down under the abuse (emotional, physical, sexual) and bullying of their leaders, or individuals destroyed by abuse of various drugs. And of course, the Manson family came out of the hippie culture as well. The Manson example is of course an extreme one, but many hippie communes self destructed for very real reasons. It's perfectly fine in your game to say, &quot;Well, that isn't truly hippie culture because it's not what I consider to be part of it&quot;; but those elements are still proof that the corruption of the Wyrm can strike anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Non sarcasm, sincerity mode) That was enlightening; Thank You. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Come to think about it; even films like Forrest Gump showed rather graphically, through Jenny Gump, how *FAR* a Hippy can fall if he/she cannot reconcile a healthy balance between his/her ideals and the pain of reality. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> That said (I apologize if my romanticized view is colored by the fact Mom was a supporter of Hippy Culture), even though they may often fall, to sincerely believe that Love Can Save The World is a notion that's still worthy of respect. Even the W20 Rulebook stated (in the &quot;Ronin&quot; Section) that &quot;At It's Core, Werewolf is a Game About Hope&quot;, and odd as it may sound, to me the protest-era songs of &quot;The Beatles&quot; (particularly those by Mr Lennon in his solo-career) are more &quot;Werewolf&quot; than Heavy Metal Songs ever will be.<br /> <br /> Then again, point taken, fail to reconcile your ideals with reality, and the Wyrm will take you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}